cff-version: 1.2.0
title: foodnet
message: "If you use foodnet, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "KU Leuven, Laboratory of Molecular Bacteriology"
abstract: >-
  foodnet builds bipartite taxon and metabolite networks (which taxon produces and which consumes which
  compound, per growth phase) from mGrowthDB batch monocultures, and the parameters of a consumer-resource
  model.
repository-code: "https://github.com/hallucigenia-sparsa/foodnet"
url: "https://github.com/hallucigenia-sparsa/foodnet"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-08"
keywords:
  - metabolites
  - cross-feeding
  - consumer-resource model
  - mGrowthDB
  - metabolic modeling
  - open science
